<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Jefferson returns with his 14-day headache diary and is seen by Dr. Haddad of headache medicine on the same day. The bout that began three weeks ago has eased. His diary shows headache on 7 of 14 days: each attack began between nine and ten in the morning, built over an hour to a moderate or severe throbbing pain across the forehead and temples, worse with reading and climbing stairs, with sensitivity to light and noise on every headache day and nausea on four, and lasted six to ten hours, settling by evening. He had no visual or other aura. The last seven days have been headache-free. He took naproxen on four days, with metoclopramide on two, and the pain was reduced but rarely gone after two hours; he has taken no combination analgesic since intake. Counting the week before intake, he has had 13 migraine days in the past four weeks. He has been sleeping six hours, has kept to two cups of coffee and has not skipped lunch. He has had no weakness, numbness, fever or change in vision. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Diary</td><td>Headache on 7 of 14 days; morning onset, six to ten hours, throbbing, light and noise sensitivity, nausea on four days; no aura</td></tr><tr><td>Past four weeks</td><td>13 migraine days</td></tr><tr><td>Acute medicine</td><td>Naproxen on four days, metoclopramide on two; partial relief</td></tr><tr><td>Combination analgesic</td><td>None since intake</td></tr><tr><td>Red flags</td><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

